<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Hermione</h1><p class="st-meta">800 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Hermione</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Coastal city of the southern Argolid, known for its sanctuary of Demeter Chthonia and its purple dye.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Hermione lay on a peninsula at the southern tip of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argolid">Argolid</a>, facing the islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hydra-greece">Hydra</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spetses">Spetses</a>. Greek tradition held that its first people were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dryopes">Dryopes</a>, later joined by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorians">Dorians</a> from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argos">Argos</a> in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hermione was a small independent city living from fishing, farming and the production of purple dye from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrian-purple">murex</a> shells. Its sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demeter">Demeter</a> Chthonia had a festival with a famous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> sacrifice, and a nearby chasm was believed to be a short route to the underworld. The city sent ships to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-salamis">Salamis</a> in 480 BCE and was usually a member of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peloponnesian-league">Peloponnesian League</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Hermione joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaean-league">Achaean League</a> c. 229 BCE when its tyrant Xenon stepped down, and passed under Roman control in 146 BCE. The modern town of Ermioni occupies the site.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 800 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 